# Round 56 — modern positivity machinery vs real-rootedness of Ξ's Jensen polynomials

| tool | gives | missing for Ξ | verdict |
|------|-------|---------------|---------|
| Lorentzian polynomials (Brändén–Huh 2020) | ultra-log-concavity (bivariate case: ULC, i.e. Newton inequalities) | ULC ⊊ real-rooted | DEAD (Turán level only) |
| Hodge theory of matroids (AHK 2018) | log-concavity from a Kähler package | Ξ-to-matroid realization | DEAD |
| real stability, Borcea–Brändén | preservers | a stable symbol producing Ξ | DEAD |
| total positivity, ASWE theorem | PF∞ ⇔ LP for sequences | PF∞ of shifted γ-sequences ≡ RH | CIRCULAR |
| Hankel/Toeplitz moment positivity | moment problems | Toeplitz minors ≥ 0 ≡ PF∞ | CIRCULAR |
| Kazhdan–Lusztig / Soergel | positivity via categorification | categorification ⇒ real-rootedness theorem | DEAD |
| hard Lefschetz packages | log-concavity, h-polynomial real-rootedness (Brenti) | Ξ-specific package | DEAD |
| multiplier sequences, Laguerre–Pólya | higher Turán inequalities (known) | global PF∞ certificate ≡ RH | CIRCULAR |

Hierarchy: Turán (known) ⊊ higher Turán (known, Dimitrov–Lucas / GORZ) ⊊ ULC for all d ⊊ real-rooted for all d ≡ RH.
All modern positivity machinery lands at the ULC/log-concave levels.
